From 86676b778e58b555dfd30704f9cbad0201b6ddca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:35:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add bounded development runtime for V4 recovery and
 candidates

Compose explicit development-store initialization, authenticated volatile body inventory, bounded candidate selection, one-step durable recovery, terminal receipt acknowledgement and invalidity propagation under one serialized owner. Preserve selector passes during header insertion and pause inconclusive VM execution without changing the journal. Any storage ambiguity drops authority and requires a separate reopen tick before work resumes.

Keep borrowed selector/store lifetime stable across owner moves; expose bounded read-only serving and diagnostic queries without a mutable store handle. Source restoration remains retained-disk-only. Budgets report component work rather than claiming selector Get caps cover full VM, undo or storage allocations.

Validation: strict C++20 -Wall -Wextra -Werror syntax; independent Release standalone runtime plus disk-state suites 2/2 passed using monetary owner's real-block fixtures, including forks, invalid-middle restoration, J/receipt/propagation gates, host-guard pause, insertion liveness, epoch exhaustion, reentry and sync-after-success authoritative reopen. VM read-only review found no remaining concrete blocker. Only new runtime source files included; borrowed tests remain uncommitted.
